Z||000000||MR86GT||01-12-2001||07:59 AM||||I need help with the procedure to adjust the emergency brakes on my 86 GT.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||01-12-2001||08:41 AM||||Look under the rear end of the car and you'll see a cable going from one side to the other just under the cradle crossmember.  It helps to raise the car to get your hands on the cable adjusting mechanism.  Please use proper ramps or jack stands.  NEVER work under a car that is supported only by a jack.<P>This cable has a open tubular looking piece where three cables come together.  On the left side of this device there is a threaded rod with a hex nut.  This is used to take the slack out of the cable.<P>With the parking brake released turn the nut on the tubular device to increase tension in the cable assembly until the parking brake lever clicks about 8 times while setting the brake.<P>Look at the back side of the rear calipers and you'll see lever where the cable attaches.  Make sure that when the parking brake is released this lever is returned completely to the rest stop.  If it is not completely against the stop you have the cable too tight.<P>This is all from memory and is subject to my recall.  I'd suggest getting a service manual (even a $12 Haynes book from AutoZone will help) and look up the procedure there.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||01-12-2001||09:27 AM||||Hey Carrolles, you forgot the most important step.  When the threaded rod with the hex nut will not turn because it's rusted solid to the tubular-looking piece, give up, crack open a beer and order new parking brake cables from the Fiero Store.||||reg||10
